# Design tokens (registry + bridge)

Applies when editing [.cursor/design/](.cursor/design/) markdown or [services/orchestration-web/src/lib/styles/tokens.css](services/orchestration-web/src/lib/styles/tokens.css).

## Authority

1. **[.cursor/design/tokens.md](.cursor/design/tokens.md)** (and other `.cursor/design/*.md` token docs) is the **canonical registry**: token name, value, intent, usage.
2. **`tokens.css`** implements that registry as `:root` CSS custom properties.

## Rules

- **Same change set:** When adding or renaming a token, update `tokens.md` (or the relevant `.cursor/design/*.md` file) **in the same commit/PR** as `tokens.css`. Do not add a new `--*` variable in `tokens.css` without a corresponding table row (unless you add the doc row immediately in the same change).
- **Renames:** Updating a token name requires changes in `tokens.md`, `tokens.css`, and every `var(--…)` usage in `services/orchestration-web`.
- **Components** must not introduce literal palette or spacing values except via `var(--…)`; literals belong only in the registry files above.
